  "label": "User projected onto the dismissive authority figure embodied by Tom Hardy",
  "description": "The user is projected onto Tom_Hardy, who is visually depicted as the authoritative figure dismissing 'snowflakes'. The user identifies with or imagines themselves as the authoritative figure who rejects those perceived as easily offended, using Tom Hardy's stern expression and persona as a visual stand-in for their own stance. The text 'move along snowflake if you're easily offended' is directed at the audience, and the user is implicitly positioned as the one enforcing this boundary, projecting their own identity onto Tom Hardy's image.",
